          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 9.4,
      "end": 12.56,
      "text": "Scientific reviews analyzed over thirty years of crime statistics.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Astronomy; a translucent diagram of the phases of the Moon. Wellcome V0025021.jpg",
        "credit": "John Emslie",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Astronomy;_a_translucent_diagram_of_the_phases_of_the_Moon._Wellcome_V0025021.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 9.4,
          "end": 12.567,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 12.56,
      "end": 15.02,
      "text": "They looked for a spike during one specific moon phase.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "37. Production of phases of the moon (22126908233).jpg",
        "credit": "Community Archives",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:37._Production_of_phases_of_the_moon_(22126908233).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 12.567,
          "end": 15.033,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 15.02,
      "end": 18.42,
      "text": "Instead, they found admission rates were identical on four other days.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Rhythms and Clocks in Marine Organisms Figure 1 Solar and Lunar Cycles ma150509.f1.jpg",
        "credit": "Image in panel a created by Reto Stockli with the help of Alan Nelson, under the leadership of Fritz Hasler, and reproduced from NASA's Visible Earth catalog (https://visibleearth.nasa.gov/images/5438",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rhythms_and_Clocks_in_Marine_Organisms_Figure_1_Solar_and_Lunar_Cycles_ma150509.f1.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 15.033,
          "end": 18.433,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 18.42,
      "end": 22.3,
      "text": "The final correlation between the moon and madness is exactly zero.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "City Traffic Illuminated City Life Night City Street Night Photography Nightlife Motion (32861900291).jpg",
        "credit": "OiMax from Tokyo, Japan",
